Ship the built frontend in the repo so it works on benches that can't build

LumenPOS found on the live Frappe Cloud v14 pilot (lumenv14) that the app
installs but /lumen and /lumen/embed/<slug> 404: public/frontend and
www/lumen.html were gitignored build output, and that bench group runs Node
14.19.0 while Vite 5 needs Node 18+, so the build silently produced nothing (the
"Install Apps" step finished in 12s, far too short for yarn install + vite).
The backend worked, the page did not. Shared marketplace benches on old Node
cannot be changed by the customer, so building on install is not reliable.

Fix (the way LumenPOS ships its own POS assets): commit the built frontend.
- .gitignore no longer ignores public/frontend or www/lumen.html; both are
  tracked. A bench that CAN build regenerates the same files; a bench that
  cannot still has them. Rebuild and commit these together on every frontend
  change (a stale bundle would ship otherwise).
- Source maps stay ignored (/lumen_reports/public/frontend/**/*.map) and
  vite.config sets build.sourcemap false in intent; the committed output is
  3.5 MB, no maps.

Defence in depth: get_status now returns reason "frontend_missing" (and
can_view false) when www/lumen.html is absent, so the POS shows a clear message
instead of embedding a 404 if a build is ever missing or partial. Everything
else in the contract is unchanged.

Message to LumenPOS: handle the new reason "frontend_missing" with something
like "Lumen Reports is installed but its dashboard page is not built on this
site. Ask an administrator to rebuild it (bench build --app lumen_reports)."

Checks: dev/test_lumenpos gains a frontend_missing case (patches _frontend_built
false -> reason frontend_missing, can_view false); full suite passes on v15,
reports gate + no-bare-cache guard pass, semgrep 0.

